Sandboxed TMPDIR is now the run-private directory via CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR set during srt's serialized wrap window
- srt (`@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime`) overrides `TMPDIR` in every wrapped command to `/tmp/claude` unless the server process has `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` set; confirmed via grep it reads `process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` on the wrap path (`generateProxyEnvVars`), so no Dockerfile `/tmp/claude` fallback was needed.
- `src/server/sandbox/srt.ts`: `runSandboxedCommand(..., opts?: { tmpdir })` → `wrapUnderPolicy(command, runConfig, tmpdir)` sets `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` after acquiring the queue turn, calls `updateConfig` + `wrapWithSandbox`, and restores/deletes the previous value in `finally` before releasing; `createSandboxedBashOperations(runConfig, opts?)` forwards it. Doc comment explains why this is process-wide state living in the serialized window.
- Call sites plumb the run's tmpdir: `src/server/gate.ts`, `src/server/installGate.ts`, `src/server/acceptanceProbe.ts` (`{ tmpdir: ctx.tmpdir }`), `src/server/harness/pi.ts` (`{ tmpdir: runContext.tmpdir }`).
- `src/server/sandbox/srt.test.ts`: new `describe("runSandboxedCommand sets CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR for the wrap")` with stubbed `SandboxManager.updateConfig`/`wrapWithSandbox`, covering previously-unset and previously-set (`vi.stubEnv`) cases; no real sandbox required.
- `docs/SANDBOXING.md`: L1 section paragraph on srt's `TMPDIR` override and the `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` handling.
